{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>The sin-offering goat.</b> The goat of the additional offerings of Rosh Chodesh; and three sin-offering goats were offered on that day — the goat of the people, the goat of Nachshon, and the goat of Rosh Chodesh — and of all of them only this one was burned. And the Sages of Israel disagreed about the matter: some say it was burned because an impurity had touched it, and some say it was burned because of אֲנִינוּת — mourning — since it is קָדְשֵׁי דוֹרוֹת, communal offerings for all generations; but in קָדְשֵׁי שָׁעָה — inaugural offerings — they relied on Moses, who had told them concerning the meal-offering, ״וְאִכְלוּהָ מַצּוֹת״ (Sifra; Zevachim 101)." "<b>He inquired diligently.</b> Two inquiries: Why was this one burned? And why were those eaten? So it is in Torat Kohanim." "<b>Against Elazar and against Itamar.</b> For Aaron's honor he turned his face toward the sons and was angry (Sifra)." "<b>Saying.</b> He said to them: Answer me regarding my words (ibid.)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:05:45.216238071Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}